  "verbalization": "Funtumine is linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is known to regulate gene expression by modifying histone methyltransferases. This complex is also the target of multiple compounds, including Sophoranochromene and a structurally diverse acetate derivative, all of which are implicated in modulating PRC2 activity. The evidence suggests that Funtumine may act through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex to influence gene expression, potentially through a mechanism involving the modification of histone tails. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same complex implies that Funtumine may share a common mechanism of action with these agents, possibly by interacting with the same molecular targets or pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Funtumine exerts its effects via the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, likely by modulating PRC2 activity, which could have implications for therapeutic applications targeting gene regulation.",
